  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m with [38;5;153mselectField[39m gives the auto-submitting environment dropdown and keeps the current sort when you
    filter.
  - [38;5;153mbadge[39m covers the status chips: green, red, amber and blue.
  - [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m and [38;5;153memptyState[39m cover the header and the "No deploys in staging" message.

  So [38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m only adds the query handling and a small duration function.

  [1mTwo tasks:[0m
  1. [1mThe page and its tests[0m ([38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m plus 8 tests): the filter, both sorts, the chips, durations, the empty
     state and fallback for bad query values.
  2. [1mWiring:[0m the route, the nav link after Services, two server tests (the page and its 503), the e2e fixtures and a
     one-line README update.

  [1mSomething the spec doesn't mention:[0m the e2e tests visit every nav link against the [38;5;153mtest/e2e/fixtures/{empty,single}/[39m
  data, so adding the link requires a [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m in both folders. Without them those two tests fail. Task 2 includes
  both files.

  [1mDecisions to check, since the spec leaves them open:[0m
  - [1mQuery values:[0m [38;5;153m?sort=service|startedAt[39m. A missing or unrecognised [38;5;153m?dir=[39m means newest-first for Started and A→Z for
    Service.
  - [1mTime display:[0m the snapshot time and the Started column use the existing [38;5;153mformatTimestamp[39m (e.g. "2026-10-01 09:05
    UTC"). Services shows raw ISO timestamps instead. Sorting still uses the raw timestamps.
  - [1mEmpty snapshot:[0m with "All environments" selected and no deploys at all, the page says "No deploys".
  - [1mLong deploys:[0m they show as minutes and seconds only, e.g. "75m 3s", with no hours.

